            "review_title": "Review at Red&Round",
            "review_text": "Leean W\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam206 contributions\n1\nOne of the Best Pizzas in the City\nDec 2020\nI often frequent Red and Round m, especially at lunchtime. The pizza has to be one of the best pizzas tasted anywhere and i would say a joint first with just 2 other pizza restaurants that I love in Ho Chi Minh. It would be impossible to judge which s the best of all three, but Red and Round is definitely one of the best of the best. The base is a super tasting thin, crispy base where even the edges taste delicious. The toppings are plentiful and succulent. The lunchtime specials include a complimentary salad which is made up of a refreshing green salad with quite generous cherry tomato halves, a delicious French dressing and generous shavings of fresh parmesan cheese. Both salad and pizzas are a treat. There is a complimentary tomato sauce and dough balls to start but I must admit the sauce tastes rather just of a tomato pulp juice with a few dried herbs in it. I know it's only complimentary and therefore perhaps I shouldn't be negative but I want this to be a totally honest review. However that is very minor and does not detract from the otherwise fantastic tasting food and a 5 Star Rating overall. Recently I decided to try a pasta dish and fell back on the old trusty spaghetti bolognaise. It was also a very pleasant surprise - thin spaghetti, very tasty beef in a sauce and fresh parmesan. The bolognaise was plentiful too and made a good balance with the pasta. A couple of times after my meal the manager has offered me a complimentary Limoncello, which I believe they make on the premises, and which is delicious and a complimentary dessert made from limoncello, with a crème caramel texture but tasting of chilled limoncello. It is absolutely delightful. Final mention must be made of the super friendly helpful staff and particularly the owner, or maybe she is the manager, who always greets me by name with a warm welcoming smile, makes some small talk and checks on whether the lunch is fine. It is truly a first class experience , taste wise and service wise, at Red and Round Restaurant.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 7, 2021",
